We should make the primitive capable of saying:
“No qualifying pulse has occurred for N seconds.”
Then the state machine chooses what N means for SUBMITTING, GENERATING, COMPLETE, etc.
That gives us the thing we really wanted from the beginning:
Timeout is not “60 seconds elapsed.”
It is:
“The system has gone silent for too long despite expecting activity.”
And genuine activity moves the silence clock forward.
